# Reference only; dotnet run does not automatically load this file.
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Development
# Organization 5101; Identity 5102; Gateway 5100
ASPNETCORE_URLS=http://localhost:5101
# Set through your shell secret store, never commit actual values:
# ConnectionStrings__Identity=<separate Identity database connection>
# ConnectionStrings__Organization=<separate Organization database connection>
# Optional server-only Google handshake configuration (no real values here):
# Worktandem__Google__ClientId=<existing OAuth client>
# Worktandem__Google__ClientSecret=<server-side secret>
# Worktandem__DataProtection__KeysPath=<existing absolute shared directory>
# Worktandem__DataProtection__CertificatePath=<existing private-key PFX>
# Worktandem__DataProtection__CertificatePassword=<optional server-side password>
# Bootstrap secret is read ONLY from its server environment variable (never appsettings/browser):
# Worktandem__Bootstrap__Secret=<separately supplied high-entropy secret; remove after setup>
# Explicitly enable only after actual Google MFA/auth_time claims are verified:
# Worktandem__Google__PrivilegedAssuranceVerified=false
# Direct mTLS internal Organization caller, existing trusted PKI (no certificates generated here):
# Worktandem__Internal__OrganizationCertificateSha256=<existing client certificate SHA-256 pin>
# Organization's outbound Identity client; requires existing trusted PKI and its own protected key ring:
# Worktandem__Identity__Origin=<trusted HTTPS Identity origin, without a path>
# Worktandem__Identity__ClientCertificatePath=<existing workload private-key PFX>
# Worktandem__Identity__ClientCertificatePassword=<optional server-side password>
# Missing/unusable configuration fails closed. No real values are supplied by this file.
